      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "Consider the vector field $F=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)\\,i-y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,j+y{z}^{3}\\,k.$ \nFind $∇\\cdot F.$",
      "worked_solution": "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j+R\\,k$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the divergence of $F$ is the scalar field given by\n\n$$\n∇\\cdot F=\\text{div}\\,F=\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}+\\frac{∂R}{∂z}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}+\\frac{∂R}{∂z} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy))+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(y{z}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+3y{z}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
